          "Federal law created protection certificates and reporting systems. Surviving impressed-seamen records list names, birthplaces, ages, physical descriptions, ships, evidence of citizenship, and the outcome of applications for release. Scars, complexion, height, and witnesses could become parts of a national identity file. The archive is administrative, repetitive, and incomplete. It is also unusually close to the bodily stakes of foreign policy.",
