          "The coincidence has encouraged a clean counterfactual: if only Washington had known, there would have been no war. The remaining dispute over impressment makes that conclusion uncertain. So do party credibility, frontier violence, and the momentum of mobilization. Knowledge of the repeal would have strengthened opponents and forced the administration to reconsider the immediate case. It would not have erased the preceding five years.",
